# SPA fallback.
#
# React Router owns the URL space. Without this, a reload on `/quotations/new`
# — or any link a user pastes to a colleague — is a 404 from the host, because
# no such file exists in `dist/`.
#
# Read by Cloudflare Pages and by Netlify. `netlify.toml` states the same rule
# for Netlify; Vercel uses the `rewrites` block in `vercel.json`. All three say
# the same thing, and this file is the one Cloudflare Pages has.
#
# Status 200, not 301: the browser must KEEP the requested path so the router
# can read it. A redirect would send every deep link to `/`.
#
# A real file always wins over this rule, so it can never shadow an asset.

/*    /index.html    200
